0	section	Starting off
1	line	Player	Now I am a knight of the round table, do you have any more quests for me?
1	line	King Arthur	Aha! I'm glad you are here! I am sending out various knights on an important quest. I was wondering if you too would like to take up this quest?
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Tell me of this quest.
2	line	Player	Tell me of this quest.
2	line	King Arthur	Well, we recently found out that the Holy Grail has passed into Gielinor.
2	line	King Arthur	This is most fortuitous!
2	line	King Arthur	None of my knights ever did return with it last time. Now we have the opportunity to give it another go, maybe this time we will have more luck!
2	cond	If the player's combat level is less than 50:
3	box	Before starting this quest, be aware that your combat level is lower than the recommended level of 50.
3	action	continue
2	cond	If the player's combat level is more than 50:
3	select	Start the Holy Grail quest?
2	option	Yes.
3	line	Player	I'd enjoy trying that.
3	line	King Arthur	Go speak to Merlin. He may be able to give a better clue as to where it is now you have freed him from that crystal.
3	line	King Arthur	He has set up his workshop in the room next to the library.
3	action	end
2	option	No.
3	line	Player	I may come back and try that later.
3	line	King Arthur	Be sure that you come speak to me soon then.
3	action	end
1	option	I am weary of questing for the time being...
2	line	Player	I am weary of questing for the time being...
2	line	King Arthur	Maybe later then?
2	line	Player	Maybe so.
2	action	end
0	section	Subsequent dialogue with King Arthur
1	line	King Arthur	How goes thy quest?
1	line	Player	I am making progress, but I have not recovered the Grail yet.
1	line	King Arthur	Well, the Grail IS very elusive, it may take some perseverance.
1	line	King Arthur	As I said before, speak to Merlin in the workshop by the library.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Merlin
1	line	Player	Hello. King Arthur has sent me on a quest for the Holy Grail. He thought you could offer some assistance.
1	line	Merlin	Ah yes... the Holy Grail...
1	line	Merlin	That is a powerful artefact indeed. Returning it here would help Camelot a lot.
1	line	Merlin	Due to its nature the Holy Grail is likely to reside in a holy place.
1	line	Player	Any suggestions?
1	line	Merlin	I believe there is a holy island somewhere not far away... I'm not entirely sure... I spent too long inside that crystal! Anyway, go and talk to someone over there.
1	line	Merlin	I suppose you could also try speaking to Sir Galahad?
1	line	Merlin	He returned from the quest many years after everyone else. He seems to know something about it, but he can only speak about those experiences cryptically.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Thank you for the advice.
2	line	Player	Thank you for the advice.
2	action	end
1	option	Where can I find Sir Galahad?
2	line	Player	Where can I find Sir Galahad?
2	line	Merlin	Galahad now lives a life of religious contemplation. He lives somewhere west of McGrubor's Wood I think.
2	action	end
